WEBVTT

00:00:00.282 --> 00:00:01.529
Last video ended here.

00:00:02.212 --> 00:00:04.256
A thirty thousand dollar car loses value at

00:00:04.357 --> 00:00:06.802
fifteen percent of its current value each year.

00:00:07.504 --> 00:00:09.728
Right now, fifteen percent of thirty thousand is

00:00:09.889 --> 00:00:12.353
four thousand five hundred, so it's losing four

00:00:12.394 --> 00:00:13.756
thousand five hundred dollars a year.

00:00:14.440 --> 00:00:15.545
But the rate doesn't stay put.

00:00:16.230 --> 00:00:18.634
When the car is worth fifteen thousand, fifteen

00:00:18.675 --> 00:00:20.597
percent of that is two thousand two hundred

00:00:20.618 --> 00:00:22.962
and fifty, so it's losing value half as

00:00:23.003 --> 00:00:23.322
fast.

00:00:24.088 --> 00:00:25.620
Half the value, half the rate.

00:00:26.508 --> 00:00:29.162
So what curve flattens exactly in step with

00:00:29.203 --> 00:00:29.604
its height?

00:00:30.369 --> 00:00:32.338
And what's the car worth after eight years?

00:00:33.015 --> 00:00:34.720
When a rate of change is always the

00:00:34.761 --> 00:00:36.987
same multiple of the amount, we say the

00:00:37.028 --> 00:00:38.994
rate is proportional to the amount.

00:00:39.798 --> 00:00:40.505
Watch what that does.

00:00:41.350 --> 00:00:43.900
A lower point gets a gentler tangent, so

00:00:43.941 --> 00:00:45.587
the curve flattens as it falls.

00:00:46.491 --> 00:00:49.138
For a quantity Q changing over time t,

00:00:49.581 --> 00:00:52.188
the rule is d Q d t equals

00:00:52.329 --> 00:00:52.850
k Q.

00:00:53.693 --> 00:00:56.462
The number k is the constant of proportionality.

00:00:57.246 --> 00:00:59.851
For the car, k is minus point one

00:00:59.932 --> 00:01:00.232
five,

00:01:00.774 --> 00:01:03.520
and its unit is per year, because dollars

00:01:03.541 --> 00:01:06.527
per year divided by dollars leaves per year.

00:01:07.350 --> 00:01:10.195
If k is negative, a positive quantity shrinks,

00:01:10.677 --> 00:01:12.420
and more slowly as it gets smaller.

00:01:13.223 --> 00:01:16.230
If k is positive, it grows, and faster

00:01:16.492 --> 00:01:17.092
as it gets bigger.

00:01:17.798 --> 00:01:18.829
Here's a curve that fits.

00:01:19.436 --> 00:01:21.992
Q equals A, times e to the k

00:01:22.053 --> 00:01:22.314
t.

00:01:22.960 --> 00:01:24.271
Let's check it by substitution.

00:01:25.017 --> 00:01:27.201
From earlier, the derivative of e to the

00:01:27.242 --> 00:01:29.866
k t is k, times e to the

00:01:29.887 --> 00:01:30.407
k t.

00:01:31.009 --> 00:01:33.452
So d Q d t is A times

00:01:33.554 --> 00:01:35.837
k, e to the k t, which is

00:01:35.918 --> 00:01:37.940
k, times A e to the k t.

00:01:38.583 --> 00:01:40.289
And A e to the k t is

00:01:40.410 --> 00:01:43.100
Q itself, so d Q d t equals

00:01:43.242 --> 00:01:43.783
k Q.

00:01:44.489 --> 00:01:45.979
That works for any A.

00:01:46.907 --> 00:01:49.031
At t equals zero, e to the zero

00:01:49.172 --> 00:01:50.835
is one, so Q is A.

00:01:52.040 --> 00:01:53.445
A is the starting value.

00:01:54.209 --> 00:01:56.774
For the car, A is thirty thousand and

00:01:56.835 --> 00:01:59.039
k is minus point one five.

00:01:59.862 --> 00:02:02.085
After eight years, it's worth thirty thousand e

00:02:02.446 --> 00:02:04.810
to the minus one point two, about nine

00:02:04.831 --> 00:02:06.112
thousand and thirty-six dollars.

00:02:06.921 --> 00:02:09.711
Savings follow the same rule, with k positive.

00:02:10.473 --> 00:02:12.438
Five thousand dollars earning six percent of its

00:02:12.498 --> 00:02:14.883
current value a year, added continuously,

00:02:15.404 --> 00:02:17.749
is five thousand e to the point zero

00:02:17.829 --> 00:02:18.291
six t.

00:02:19.352 --> 00:02:22.176
After eight years, that's five thousand e to

00:02:22.196 --> 00:02:23.137
the point four eight,

00:02:23.797 --> 00:02:25.660
about eight thousand and eighty dollars.

00:02:26.429 --> 00:02:27.293
Now the shapes.

00:02:27.938 --> 00:02:30.414
Take A equals two, and change k.

00:02:31.240 --> 00:02:34.035
With k positive, the curve climbs ever more

00:02:34.097 --> 00:02:34.498
steeply.

00:02:35.202 --> 00:02:37.749
Turn k down through zero, and it becomes

00:02:37.770 --> 00:02:40.859
a flat line, then falls, flattening out as

00:02:40.920 --> 00:02:41.320
it drops.

00:02:41.963 --> 00:02:44.347
That decay curve gets closer and closer to

00:02:44.388 --> 00:02:46.992
the t axis, but never reaches it, because

00:02:47.013 --> 00:02:48.795
e to any power is positive.

00:02:49.297 --> 00:02:52.375
So Q equals zero is a horizontal asymptote.

00:02:52.999 --> 00:02:55.345
For growth, the same thing happens going back

00:02:55.406 --> 00:02:55.827
in time.

00:02:56.911 --> 00:02:58.277
Now make A negative.

00:02:59.062 --> 00:03:01.627
Every value changes sign, so the graph reflects

00:03:01.769 --> 00:03:02.570
in the t axis.

00:03:03.132 --> 00:03:05.117
It still obeys d Q d t equals

00:03:05.178 --> 00:03:07.162
k Q, with the same asymptote.

00:03:07.564 --> 00:03:10.053
But money or mass can't be negative, so

00:03:10.195 --> 00:03:12.564
models use a positive A, and t from

00:03:12.625 --> 00:03:13.086
zero on.

00:03:13.548 --> 00:03:16.015
Often k isn't given, so we find it

00:03:16.056 --> 00:03:16.597
from data.

00:03:17.140 --> 00:03:19.107
A town had ten thousand people in twenty

00:03:19.149 --> 00:03:21.538
ten, and twelve thousand in twenty fifteen.

00:03:22.221 --> 00:03:24.627
Assuming the growth is proportional, when will it

00:03:24.668 --> 00:03:25.871
reach twenty thousand?

00:03:26.614 --> 00:03:28.683
Let t be the years after twenty ten,

00:03:29.006 --> 00:03:30.552
so A is ten thousand.

00:03:31.276 --> 00:03:34.202
At t equals five, twelve thousand equals ten

00:03:34.243 --> 00:03:35.826
thousand e to the five k.

00:03:36.509 --> 00:03:38.598
Divide by ten thousand, so e to the

00:03:38.639 --> 00:03:40.266
five k is one point two.

00:03:40.991 --> 00:03:42.708
Take the natural log of both sides.

00:03:43.392 --> 00:03:45.454
Five k is the natural log of one

00:03:45.495 --> 00:03:46.075
point two,

00:03:46.617 --> 00:03:48.619
so k is the natural log of one

00:03:48.660 --> 00:03:50.021
point two, over five,

00:03:50.563 --> 00:03:53.145
about point zero three six five per year.

00:03:53.856 --> 00:03:55.890
Now set P to twenty thousand.

00:03:56.515 --> 00:03:58.942
Dividing by ten thousand gives e to the

00:03:58.983 --> 00:04:00.246
k t equals two.

00:04:01.030 --> 00:04:02.756
So k t is the natural log of

00:04:02.797 --> 00:04:02.997
two,

00:04:03.620 --> 00:04:05.587
and t is the natural log of two,

00:04:05.889 --> 00:04:06.270
over k.

00:04:07.093 --> 00:04:09.136
That's five times the natural log of two,

00:04:09.618 --> 00:04:11.400
over the natural log of one point two,

00:04:12.002 --> 00:04:13.664
about nineteen point zero years.

00:04:14.607 --> 00:04:14.766
So,

00:04:15.309 --> 00:04:18.214
if the growth stays proportional, the population reaches

00:04:18.275 --> 00:04:20.520
twenty thousand during twenty twenty-nine.

00:04:21.343 --> 00:04:24.190
Keep k exact until the end, so rounding

00:04:24.231 --> 00:04:24.772
doesn't creep in.

00:04:25.481 --> 00:04:27.889
Decay works the same way, with k negative.

00:04:28.612 --> 00:04:31.141
A substance has a half-life of twelve years.

00:04:31.704 --> 00:04:33.952
That means every twelve years, the amount halves.

00:04:34.615 --> 00:04:35.884
Start with two hundred grams.

00:04:36.386 --> 00:04:38.450
After twelve years there are a hundred grams,

00:04:38.790 --> 00:04:41.195
so a hundred equals two hundred e to

00:04:41.215 --> 00:04:41.857
the twelve k.

00:04:42.619 --> 00:04:44.483
That gives e to the twelve k equals

00:04:44.525 --> 00:04:44.965
a half,

00:04:45.467 --> 00:04:47.713
so twelve k is the natural log of

00:04:47.754 --> 00:04:49.979
a half, which is minus the natural log

00:04:50.000 --> 00:04:50.340
of two.

00:04:51.104 --> 00:04:52.947
So k is minus the natural log of

00:04:53.048 --> 00:04:54.089
two, over twelve,

00:04:54.672 --> 00:04:56.315
and that minus sign is the decay.

00:04:57.255 --> 00:04:59.577
After thirty years, Q is two hundred e

00:04:59.917 --> 00:05:02.058
to the thirty k, which is two hundred

00:05:02.118 --> 00:05:03.579
times two to the minus two and a

00:05:03.619 --> 00:05:06.000
half, about thirty-five point four grams.

00:05:06.635 --> 00:05:08.763
Here's a pattern that checks answers like these.

00:05:09.469 --> 00:05:10.073
Equal times,

00:05:10.618 --> 00:05:11.242
equal factors.

00:05:11.987 --> 00:05:14.511
In any five years, the town multiplies by

00:05:14.612 --> 00:05:17.357
one point two, wherever it starts, because e

00:05:17.398 --> 00:05:19.401
to the five k is one point two.

00:05:20.062 --> 00:05:23.543
So ten thousand becomes twelve thousand, then fourteen

00:05:23.584 --> 00:05:26.345
thousand four hundred, and so on, passing twenty

00:05:26.366 --> 00:05:28.126
thousand just before twenty thirty.

00:05:28.868 --> 00:05:31.436
And every twelve years, the substance halves.

00:05:32.139 --> 00:05:34.266
Thirty years is two and a half half-lives,

00:05:34.609 --> 00:05:37.338
so the answer sits between fifty and twenty-five

00:05:37.379 --> 00:05:37.699
grams.

00:05:38.504 --> 00:05:40.832
This only works while k stays constant.

00:05:43.462 --> 00:05:43.846
Your turn.

00:05:44.531 --> 00:05:46.798
A population of eight hundred grows at a

00:05:46.878 --> 00:05:49.506
rate proportional to its size, and doubles in

00:05:49.586 --> 00:05:50.167
ten years.

00:05:50.809 --> 00:05:53.397
Find the exact value of k, and the

00:05:53.437 --> 00:05:56.345
population after fifteen years, to the nearest whole

00:05:56.405 --> 00:05:56.666
number.

00:05:57.187 --> 00:05:58.156
Pause here to answer.

00:06:09.040 --> 00:06:12.122
Doubling means sixteen hundred equals eight hundred e

00:06:12.182 --> 00:06:13.263
to the ten k,

00:06:13.764 --> 00:06:15.765
so e to the ten k is two,

00:06:16.285 --> 00:06:18.407
and k is the natural log of two,

00:06:18.787 --> 00:06:19.287
over ten.

00:06:20.288 --> 00:06:23.035
After fifteen years, P is eight hundred times

00:06:23.175 --> 00:06:25.079
two to the one and a half, about

00:06:25.220 --> 00:06:27.064
two thousand two hundred and sixty-three.

00:06:27.686 --> 00:06:30.674
It's not twenty-four hundred, halfway between sixteen hundred

00:06:30.735 --> 00:06:31.657
and thirty-two hundred.

00:06:32.281 --> 00:06:33.475
Growth isn't a straight line.

00:06:35.231 --> 00:06:35.634
Last one.

00:06:36.519 --> 00:06:38.840
A one hundred gram sample decays at a

00:06:38.941 --> 00:06:41.883
rate proportional to its mass, with a half-life

00:06:41.984 --> 00:06:42.864
of five years.

00:06:43.586 --> 00:06:45.327
Find the mass after ten years,

00:06:45.869 --> 00:06:47.550
and the rate of change of the mass

00:06:47.751 --> 00:06:49.653
at that time, with units.

00:06:50.397 --> 00:06:51.724
Pause here to answer.

00:07:02.355 --> 00:07:05.322
Ten years is two half-lives, so a quarter

00:07:05.384 --> 00:07:06.787
is left, twenty-five grams.

00:07:07.509 --> 00:07:09.773
With k equal to minus the natural log

00:07:09.814 --> 00:07:12.518
of two, over five, the rate is k

00:07:12.580 --> 00:07:13.561
times the mass now.

00:07:14.242 --> 00:07:16.984
So d Q d t is minus five

00:07:17.045 --> 00:07:18.445
times the natural log of two,

00:07:19.126 --> 00:07:21.527
about minus three point four seven grams per

00:07:21.588 --> 00:07:21.867
year.

00:07:22.689 --> 00:07:25.197
Using the starting hundred grams gives minus thirteen

00:07:25.238 --> 00:07:25.879
point nine.

00:07:26.463 --> 00:07:28.309
That's the rate at the start, not at

00:07:28.350 --> 00:07:28.811
ten years.

00:07:30.501 --> 00:07:32.985
So a rate that's proportional to the amount

00:07:33.146 --> 00:07:35.410
gives exponential growth or decay,

00:07:35.991 --> 00:07:38.576
and the starting value picks one curve out

00:07:38.596 --> 00:07:39.137
of the family.

00:07:40.180 --> 00:07:42.389
Next, we run differentiation backwards.

00:07:43.192 --> 00:07:45.274
If f prime of x is two x,

00:07:45.755 --> 00:07:47.356
which functions could f be,

00:07:47.917 --> 00:07:50.059
and how does one condition pick out just

00:07:50.179 --> 00:07:50.540
one of them?

00:07:53.268 --> 00:07:54.070
Here are the key notes.

00:07:54.714 --> 00:07:56.441
Pause the video if you need more time

00:07:56.503 --> 00:07:56.984
to copy them.
